{"html": "<div class=\"kicker\">Bedford + Bowery — June 17, 2014</div>\n    <h1>Watch Members of MGMT, Louis XIV and More Cut a Record For a New Vinyl Club</h1>\n    <div class=\"byline\">By Andrew Alexander · Bedford + Bowery</div>\n    <p>Two brothers in Brooklyn are bringing back the days of mail-order record clubs, building on the concept, and having fun in the process of doing so. Albert and Philip Di Fiore run a studio in Brooklyn called The Rumpus Room where Caveman, Sinkane, Eleanor Friedberger, and Rumors have all recorded. The space is now also home to monthly recording parties curated by the ambitious siblings, as well as musician Jon Wiley. “The idea with these parties is to host a bunch of musicians at the studio who are creative and interesting people,” Philip told B+B over pizza and beer at the most recent recording party. “We eat, have a few drinks, socialize and then make crazy music. One of my favorite parts of the parties is that musicians who haven’t met get to know each other in a very loose and fun situation.”</p>\n    <p>Each session is recorded live, with Albert as the producer, to a 24-track tape machine. From there the album gets mixed, also live with the hands of multiple people on the mixers, to a 2-track tape machine. The music then makes its way to the studio of Josh Bonati, who masters it directly from the tape before cutting and sending it to the pressing plant to be turned into vinyl. Not once does the music touch any digital program. “It’s an old jazz concept: Work quickly, and have a high quality about it where it’s not sterile,” explained Philip.</p>\n    <p>On the first of each month, club members will receive a limited edition, monochromatic vinyl with a white cover sporting only the name of the band. Aesthetics are key to Philip, whose main gig is as a director (his work includes countless music videos, and the rockumentary Stranger: Bernie Worrell on Earth). The albums will also be sold in various record stores. Details—such as which record stores will carry the albums, and the price of membership—are still being discussed.</p>\n    <p>“I think people are going to be impressed. Musicians they may know are making wild music, without worrying about their own bands’ style, record labels, critics, or popular opinion. They can just be completely free and when creative people are free, special things can happen. We just try to create a fun atmosphere and document it,” said Philip. “It’s a bigger project than just music. It’s a real representation of New York City art.”</p>\n    <div class=\"press-gallery\">\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/01.jpg\" alt=\"Master of Ceremonies, Philip Di Fiore.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Master of Ceremonies, Philip Di Fiore.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/02.jpg\" alt=\"Producer and co-founder of the record club, Albert Di Fiore.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Producer and co-founder of the record club, Albert Di Fiore.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/03.jpg\" alt=\"Jon Wiley (Adam Green, Lightspeed Champion, The Honorary Title) on drums.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jon Wiley (Adam Green, Lightspeed Champion, The Honorary Title) on drums.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/04.jpg\" alt=\"James Pollis playing guitar. Pollis previously recorded at The Rumpus Room with his band See Through.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>James Pollis playing guitar. Pollis previously recorded at The Rumpus Room with his band See Through.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/05.jpg\" alt=\"James Richardson (MGMT, Kuroma) playing guitar.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>James Richardson (MGMT, Kuroma) playing guitar.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/06.jpg\" alt=\"Jason Hill (Louis XIV, The Killers, The Virgins) on guitar.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jason Hill (Louis XIV, The Killers, The Virgins) on guitar.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/07.jpg\" alt=\"Darwin Smith (Darwin Deez) playing guitar.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Darwin Smith (Darwin Deez) playing guitar.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/08.jpg\" alt=\"Gregory Richardson (Darwin Deez) on drums.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Gregory Richardson (Darwin Deez) on drums.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/09.jpg\" alt=\"Jon Cowherd, legendary jazz musician, playing piano.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jon Cowherd, legendary jazz musician, playing piano.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/10.jpg\" alt=\"Andrew Borger (Tom Waits, Norah Jones, Ani DiFranco) playing drums.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Andrew Borger (Tom Waits, Norah Jones, Ani DiFranco) playing drums.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/11.jpg\" alt=\"Don De Vore (Amazing Baby) making magic happen.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Don De Vore (Amazing Baby) making magic happen.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/12.jpg\" alt=\"Ari Ingber (Showgirls) on keys.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Ari Ingber (Showgirls) on keys.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/13.jpg\" alt=\"Emma Gomis (Esther Creative Group) on bass.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Emma Gomis (Esther Creative Group) on bass.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/14.jpg\" alt=\"Michael Rosen (Icewater) on keys.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Michael Rosen (Icewater) on keys.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/15.jpg\" alt=\"James Richardson mastering the trumpet. Ari Ingber, Emma Gomis, and Jason Hill in the background.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>James Richardson mastering the trumpet. Ari Ingber, Emma Gomis, and Jason Hill in the background.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/16.jpg\" alt=\"Sisters Emma and Andrea Gomis team up on piano.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Sisters Emma and Andrea Gomis team up on piano.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/17.jpg\" alt=\"Jon Cowherd on piano, with Darwin Smith, Michael Rosen, and James Pollis in the background.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jon Cowherd on piano, with Darwin Smith, Michael Rosen, and James Pollis in the background.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/18.jpg\" alt=\"Jason Hill and Darwin Smith.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jason Hill and Darwin Smith.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/19.jpg\" alt=\"Jon Wiley plays guitar while Ari Ingber plays the keyboard.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jon Wiley plays guitar while Ari Ingber plays the keyboard.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/20.jpg\" alt=\"Jason Hill.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Jason Hill.</figcaption></figure>\n    <figure class=\"press-figure\"><img src=\"/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/img/21.jpg\" alt=\"Gregory Richardson at the piano.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Gregory Richardson at the piano.</figcaption></figure>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"source-note\">\n      Originally published by Bedford + Bowery, June 17, 2014. Archived via the\n      <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20140702144117/https://bedfordandbowery.com/2014/06/watch-members-of-mgmt-louis-xiv-and-more-put-a-party-on-vinyl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Wayback Machine</a>.\n    </div>", "source": "/press/bedford-bowery-recording-parties/"}